  "title": "Kourovka problem 12.6 (main)",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "pdf-text-entry",
    "text": "Let G be a finitely generated group and suppose that H is a p-subgroup of\nG such that H contains no non-trivial normal subgroups of G and HX = XH for\nany subgroup X of G. Is then G/CG (H G ) a p-group where H G is the normal closure\nof H?                                                                  G. Busetto",
